{#-
  The wrap-up's request, sent at the end of a scene's session once the scene has ended
  (procreator/folds.ts). Procreator saves everything the scene established, then writes its
  summary, which every brief from then on holds. The task comes last, after the session. Takes the
  scene's number.
-#}
<wrap_up>
Scene {{ scene }} has ended. This session closes after this, and the next scene starts from a new brief.

First, save. Make sure the reference holds everything this scene established that will matter later: write or edit the pages it belongs on (characters, places, groups, things, the world), shift the relationships that changed, and bring Threads, Timeline and Plan up to date. Put what you've learned about the owner or the work in your memory. Skip what's saved already.

Then write the scene's summary for the story so far, which every brief from now on holds. It's the story's backbone and the pages hold the detail, so keep to what someone following the whole story needs: what happened, what changed between people, what was revealed and to whom, and how things stand at the end. Usually 100 to 250 words.

After your tool calls, answer with the summary and nothing else: plain prose, past tense, people by name.
</wrap_up>
